---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import MortgageCalculator from '../components/tools/MortgageCalculator.svelte';
import PrivacyNote from '../components/PrivacyNote.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Mortgage Calculator"
  description="Estimate your monthly mortgage payment, see a breakdown of principal, interest, tax, insurance, PMI, and HOA fees, and view a yearly amortization schedule."
>
  <h1 class="mb-1 text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Mortgage Calculator</h1>
  <PrivacyNote text="Runs entirely in your browser. No data is ever transmitted to our servers." />

  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <MortgageCalculator client:load />
  </div>

  <section class="mt-10 max-w-2xl text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
    <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">About this tool</h2>
    <p class="mb-2">
      Principal & interest is calculated with the standard amortization formula: <code>M = P × [r(1+r)ⁿ] / [(1+r)ⁿ − 1]</code>, where <code>P</code> is the loan amount, <code>r</code> is the monthly interest rate, and <code>n</code> is the number of monthly payments. Property tax, homeowner's insurance, PMI, and HOA fees are optional and added on top as flat monthly amounts.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Amortization tab shows how much of each year's payments goes toward principal versus
      interest, and your remaining loan balance. Early payments are mostly interest, and that
      shifts toward principal as the loan matures.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
